   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Line Boil\n\nA hand-drawn outline draws itself, boils on threes like a cel animation, and fills with color while it keeps boiling. Takes any closed outline as SVG path data in the path variable (default: a five-point star).\n\nCategory: graphic-looks. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A simple mark, icon or shape should feel hand-animated, with the restless line of traditional cel animation.\n- A playful explainer or kids-friendly scene needs a hero shape that draws itself and then stays alive on screen.\n- You have the shape as SVG path data and want it drawn, filled and boiling without keyframing anything.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The thing being drawn is a word or a font's glyph outlines: use outline-trace.\n- The line should circle or mark up an existing part of the frame rather than be the subject: use scribble-circle.\n- Existing content should just feel hand-placed and jittery, without being redrawn: use paper-wobble.\n\nVariables:\n- path (string): Path, default \"M 100.00 0.00 L 123.51 67.64 L 195.11 69.10 L 138.04 112.36 L 158.78 180.90 L 100.00 140.00 L 41.22 180.90 L 61.96 112.36 L 4.89 69.10 L 76.49 67.64 Z\"\n- boil_every (number, 1-8): Boil every, default 3\n- drawings (number, 1-8): Drawings, default 3\n- amplitude (number, 0-3): Wobble, default 1\n- stroke_width (number, 2-24): Line weight, default 9\n- size (number, 0.2-0.9): Size, default 0.66\n- line (color): Line, default \"#111111\"\n- fill (color): Fill, default \"#E5322D\"\n- background (color): Background, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- speed (number, 0.1-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
